WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.879
- West Palm Beach is just a

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:06.131
place that hits home to me.

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:07.382
It's where it all started.

00:00:07.382 --> 00:00:09.634
I remember when I was just goin’ in,

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:10.802
just hoop, tryna have fun.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.595
And you were just young. You have

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:14.514
a dream, and it's just, like, you're just

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.307
trying to achieve whatever you can do.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:18.727
So you just went outside late at night,

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:21.104
going to the park, tryna go hoop, tryna go grind.

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.695
- If I could start with this acai bowl.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.571
- Yeah, you know, I’m eating healthy now.

00:00:29.571 --> 00:00:32.282
- Yeah.
- Come on, I’m trying to get big. Stay in shape.

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:35.035
The acai bowl. As you can see, the

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.537
strawberries with bananas.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.539
I think that’s oats. And you got a little bit of

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:43.835
honey in it. It’s fire, you know.
It’s been my go-to.

00:00:43.835 --> 00:00:45.253
It's pretty good though.

00:00:45.253 --> 00:00:46.546
No cap.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.590
Look at that. Come on, get a
good look at that.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.133
Growing up, my mom raised me by

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:51.718
herself, and she always tried to do

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.636
stuff for me and my two brothers and

00:00:53.636 --> 00:00:55.638
one sister. To see how hard she works,

00:00:55.638 --> 00:00:56.765
that pushes me.

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:58.892
You just wanna help your family out,

00:00:58.892 --> 00:00:59.851
give back to them,

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:01.061
cuz they put so much

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.103
time and effort into you.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:05.482
If you was to ask me what my dream is, I just,

00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:08.068
as a kid, you know, you always had to have a dream

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:09.652
I just grew up watching basketball.

00:01:10.862 --> 00:01:12.572
So it's always been a dream of mine.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.865
One of my proudest achievements

00:01:13.865 --> 00:01:15.033
was winning my first gold medal,

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:15.950
U16.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:17.786
I feel like it opened up a lot for me.

00:01:17.786 --> 00:01:20.163
It was me, James Wiseman, Vernon

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:22.665
Carey, Jalen Green, Jalen Suggs.

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:24.250
I never expected that in my life.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.002
So it was just crazy to me.

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:27.462
People started looking at me more.

00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:29.339
Started blowin’ up after that.
- [Announcer:] Here’s Barnes now.

00:01:29.339 --> 00:01:32.675
Down the lane, and it goes.

00:01:32.675 --> 00:01:35.178
- [Announcer:] And he just is so long.
Elongates to the rim there in

00:01:35.178 --> 00:01:36.679
the open court.
- Jumping into that system,

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:38.306
I knew that was the right fit for me.

00:01:38.306 --> 00:01:40.016
Just when I watched the program, they had

00:01:40.016 --> 00:01:41.976
said they wanted me to do—talk to coaches.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:45.522
I already knew what it was from the jump.

00:01:45.522 --> 00:01:47.190
So that just allowed me

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.025
to go in there, be who I am.

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:51.402
- [Announcer:] Oh! That's what you're

00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:52.487
talking about right there.

00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:54.239
Scottie Barnes.
- During the season, it

00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:56.116
was, I would say it was very different.

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:59.077
Plenty of teammates getting COVID, and then you

00:01:59.077 --> 00:02:00.286
gotta sit out two weeks.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.204
Can't play a game.

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:04.040
That was very weird, you know? It's

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.625
just like you always on your toes.

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:16.678
- Scottie first came out to Santa Barbara, and we

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:18.221
got in the gym to kinda evaluate his

00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:20.306
game and where he's at. The first thing,

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.225
you know, we had done ahead of time

00:02:22.225 --> 00:02:23.768
was go over film and kind of prepare

00:02:23.768 --> 00:02:25.436
for him, and his ability to be, you

00:02:25.436 --> 00:02:27.689
know, a big point forward and be able

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:29.691
to just create for everybody else

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:30.358
is so obvious.

00:02:33.194 --> 00:02:34.237
- I’m just trying to make the right

00:02:34.237 --> 00:02:35.238
play each and every time.

00:02:35.238 --> 00:02:37.407
So if play’s open, I'm trying

00:02:37.407 --> 00:02:39.117
to find that play and see what’s the right

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:40.785
decision to make.
- [Trner:] The big thing we wanted

00:02:40.785 --> 00:02:42.954
to really work on, you know, further developing

00:02:42.954 --> 00:02:44.372
his jump shot and his confidence in it.

00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:46.082
He’s just such a pass-first guy

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:47.333
that it’s getting him to understand,

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.085
like, sometimes the best option is

00:02:49.085 --> 00:02:51.254
him taking that shot.
Full extension,

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:53.089
full extension, full extension.

00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:57.594
Yes, sir.
- I like Packie.

00:02:57.594 --> 00:02:58.720
Cool, fun dude.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.138
- Nice guy to talk to as well.

00:03:00.138 --> 00:03:02.515
- [Barnes:] Taught me a lot about my shot.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.518
Helped me get my general feeling
from where I’m starting from

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.061
to where I’m goin’

00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:08.479
just helps me get better.
- [Turner:] Setting a number

00:03:08.479 --> 00:03:09.731
for him or giving him, “Hey, we're

00:03:09.731 --> 00:03:11.691
trying to go five out of seven” or

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.776
“three for five” or “seven out of 10,”

00:03:13.776 --> 00:03:15.612
you know, it’s just giving him a goal.

00:03:15.612 --> 00:03:16.988
He's a competitor.

00:03:16.988 --> 00:03:18.531
So he always rises to the occasion

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:20.408
and wants to go until he can get it.

00:03:21.409 --> 00:03:23.203
- Let's go. Look at the boys.

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:23.995
Look at them boys.

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:29.792
P3 boys right there.
- Those are P3 boys right there?
- Look at them.
[Honking horn]

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:34.172
Hey, guys!

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:36.758
So we at P3 right now.

00:03:36.758 --> 00:03:38.426
We about to get the arms, shoulders

00:03:38.426 --> 00:03:39.135
right.

00:03:39.135 --> 00:03:41.054
Think it's arm day.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:45.016
So we ‘bout to hit it. ‘Bout to
meet the crew.

00:03:45.016 --> 00:03:46.100
- I mean, the idea behind

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.727
P3 was that we could

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:49.520
collect more data on athletes.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.855
We could have them have this interaction

00:03:50.855 --> 00:03:52.774
with technology that would give us

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:54.734
information about how these guys

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.527
move, how their bodies work, how

00:03:56.527 --> 00:03:58.488
their systems are put together

00:03:58.488 --> 00:03:59.447
so we can take better care of them.

00:03:59.948 --> 00:04:01.741
And so when we assess an athlete like

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:04.452
Scottie Barnes, we can compare his system

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:06.246
to all the physical systems that he's

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:08.122
gonna be competing against in the NBA.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.540
- [Barnes:] Developed my muscles

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.333
at P3.

00:04:10.333 --> 00:04:11.542
And now we’ve just been training and

00:04:11.542 --> 00:04:13.336
working on different things.

00:04:13.336 --> 00:04:15.546
Helping me jump better. Not doing so

00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:18.758
much to try to get us all big and strong,

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:23.972
but just to maintain and make us feel good.
That’s why I like it.

00:04:23.972 --> 00:04:26.641
I feel like after P3, you could
just go hoop on the court.

00:04:26.641 --> 00:04:27.850
They keep us right.

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.811
- We’ve had Scottie for three years now.

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:30.812
Pretty much all of these top

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:32.355
young players find their way to P3

00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:33.982
before they get to the NBA now.

00:04:34.565 --> 00:04:36.359
And so we can track their—not

00:04:36.359 --> 00:04:37.777
just their—how their physical

00:04:37.777 --> 00:04:39.779
system looks at one point in time,

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.864
but we can track their development cycle.

00:04:41.864 --> 00:04:43.783
Scottie is a really good athlete.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:44.575
These last two years,

00:04:44.575 --> 00:04:46.119
he's made huge gains.

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.954
Like, much steeper growth

00:04:47.954 --> 00:04:50.248
curve than most of our young athletes.

00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:52.083
And this time when we assessed him, his

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:53.960
drop vertical was the second-highest

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.795
we'd ever measured, with comps from

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.463
almost 900 NBA players that we've

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.382
assessed. The second-highest jump ever.

00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:01.384
Like, that's—it was phenomenal.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:05.930
- Scott,

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.849
I’ll give you five bucks if you eat that one.

00:05:07.849 --> 00:05:09.100
- Bro, I don’t even know what that is.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.145
- I’ll give you 10.
- I don’t know what that is, though.

00:05:12.145 --> 00:05:13.104
- Twenty.

00:05:13.104 --> 00:05:13.938
- What is that?
- Twenty. $20.

00:05:14.147 --> 00:05:17.608
I'll give you $20. I’m not
about to feed you!

00:05:17.608 --> 00:05:20.445
- No, I wanna smell it.

00:05:20.445 --> 00:05:24.949
Bro, that smells terrible. What the heck?
- Bro, I’ll give you 20. I’ll give you $20.
- I might throw up if I eat that.

00:05:24.949 --> 00:05:26.659
- I’ll give you $20 if you can eat this.
- I can’t.

00:05:26.659 --> 00:05:29.412
I'm bad at trying new foods.
Greg’s like family.

00:05:29.412 --> 00:05:31.956
We like cousins, to be honest.
We lit, though.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.168
He my hype man, I’m his hype man.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:37.253
He’s lit. I like Greg.

00:05:37.253 --> 00:05:38.671
Let’s go! Good defense, KD!

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:41.132
There was four people guarding this man

00:05:41.132 --> 00:05:42.842
when he tried to bring it up in transition.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:43.885
Come on, man.

00:05:43.885 --> 00:05:46.596
That's how you know he’s like that.
Bro, go set

00:05:46.596 --> 00:05:49.307
a double-down screen for KD.

00:05:49.307 --> 00:05:58.399
That’s a tough guard.
- Tough cover. Very tough cover.
- I’d rather guard Giannis than KD.
- Yeah.

00:05:59.609 --> 00:06:03.780
- Bruh, just give it to KD.
Oh! 

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:11.454
Oh, y'all ahead.
- [Offscreen:] Oh, I’m sorry.
- Wait, what?
- Oh, they ahead of us.

00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:16.959
Come on. What we on, what we on?
He made that.
- That’s game.

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:26.177
- That’s a wrap.
- Man, Santa Barbara. Man, the beach—sunset.
It’s nice out

00:06:26.177 --> 00:06:28.304
here, baby. Livin’ life.

00:06:30.515 --> 00:06:32.183
Me, I just want to win games. If
I need to

00:06:32.183 --> 00:06:34.310
play power forward, help my team get

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:36.104
rebounds, push the transition,

00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:37.188
that's what I do.

00:06:37.188 --> 00:06:38.189
If I need the ball in my hands

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:40.316
to create, look for open people, get

00:06:40.316 --> 00:06:43.319
shooters involved, things like that,
be a slasher—

00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:44.237
whatever's needed,

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:45.905
that's what I'm willing to do

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:47.573
to try to win basketball games.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:48.574
- I see Scottie’s role in the

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:50.493
NBA evolving really right on

00:06:50.493 --> 00:06:51.536
point with the times, right?

00:06:51.536 --> 00:06:53.621
He's positionless, so Scottie really fits

00:06:53.621 --> 00:06:56.124
with today's NBA and the ability to be

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:57.917
anywhere and everywhere at the same time.

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.836
- If you take a guy that has the work

00:06:59.836 --> 00:07:02.130
ethic that Scottie has and you give

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:04.757
him the right blueprint to get better,

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.342
then, you know, he's gonna just

00:07:06.342 --> 00:07:08.219
keep going.
- Whatever fanbase it is,

00:07:08.219 --> 00:07:09.637
you know, I'm just gonna

00:07:09.637 --> 00:07:11.597
come in working hard from day one..

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:12.598
I'mma come in with the

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.225
right mindset, right approach.

00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:15.685
I feel like it's gonna be a good vibe,

00:07:15.685 --> 00:07:17.395
you know? I'mma have fun.

00:07:17.395 --> 00:07:18.938
They gonna have fun in the crowd.

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.273
It's gonna be a perfect combination.

00:07:21.649 --> 00:07:22.275
Of course it’ll be

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:23.234
a pretty special moment.

00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:24.068
It's gonna be one of the biggest

00:07:24.068 --> 00:07:25.945
moments of my life, everything that I've been

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.781
working for. I don’t know if I’ll cry.

00:07:28.781 --> 00:07:29.699
I’m probably gonna scream.

00:07:30.533 --> 00:07:34.287
“Ahhh, let’s go!”
Still got a long way to go.

00:07:34.287 --> 00:07:35.705
It ain’t over yet. I feel like it’s

00:07:35.705 --> 00:07:37.957
just one step. A big part of you

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:39.959
getting there, but you gotta do things

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:40.710
to stay there.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:41.878
You can't just get there

00:07:41.878 --> 00:07:43.045
and then think it's over.

00:07:43.045 --> 00:07:44.422
You got way more of the

00:07:44.422 --> 00:07:45.715
journey that we've got to go.

00:07:45.715 --> 00:07:46.841
I just wanna leave that legacy that

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:49.969
Scottie Barnes was one of those

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.554
guys that was just a different

00:07:51.554 --> 00:07:53.973
type of guy that studied the game,

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:55.850
that I did whatever I could.

